-- title:
--   Convergence of Fontaine's w-series when c_k ∈ pg eventually
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $g$ a commutative ring which is adically complete with respect to the ideal $\mathrm{span}\{p\} = pg$ (in Mathlib's sense: both separated and precomplete for the $pg$-adic filtration). Let $c : \mathbb{N} \to g$ be a sequence for which there exists $n$ with $c_k \in pg$ for all $k \ge n$. In the localisation $g[1/p] =$ `Localization.Away (p : g)`, where the image of $p$ is a unit, write `invPow p g m` for the $m$-th power of the inverse of that unit, and set $$\mathrm{wPartialSum}_p(c)(N) = \sum_{k < N} (\text{image of } p)^{-k} \cdot c_k^{p^k},$$ the image of $c_k^{p^k}$ being taken under the structure map $g \to g[1/p]$. Let $\mathrm{wSeries}_p(c)$ be the element of $g[1/p]$ defined as a choice of $p$-adic limit of these partial sums if one exists, and $0$ otherwise, where an element $\alpha$ is a $p$-adic limit of a sequence $u$ when for every $s$ there is $n_0$ with $u_n - \alpha$ in the $g$-submodule of $g[1/p]$ generated by the image of $p^s$, for all $n \ge n_0$. The conclusion is that $\mathrm{wSeries}_p(c)$ is such a $p$-adic limit of $\mathrm{wPartialSum}_p(c)$; in particular a limit does exist, so the value is not the default $0$.
--
--   This is the convergence statement for Fontaine's series $\sum_k p^{-k} c_k^{p^k}$ underlying the comparison between Honda systems and $p$-divisible groups, in the case where the coefficients eventually lie in $pg$. It is used in the construction and characterisation of coordinates on the Fontaine functor, in particular in the results on split coordinates and on membership in the Fontaine functor.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Deformation_PLoc_isPadicLimit_wPartialSum_wSeries_of_eventually_mem_span.lean

